<title>USA: Manufactured Homes replaces accountants.</title>
<headline>Manufactured Homes replaces accountants.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manufactured Home Communities Inc said it has dismissed  Coopers &amp; Lybrand LLP as its independent public accountants and replaced the firm with Ernst &amp; Young LLP.</p>
<p>The move was effective October 8, according to a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for Manufactured Home, a real estate investment trust, said the company made the switch because it wanted an accountant with more real estate investment trust experience.</p>
<p>Manufactured Homes is in the midst of a hostile tender offer for Chateau Properties Inc, but the spokeswoman said that offer had nothing to do with the change of accountants.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
